e sum find the product  and then multiply the left-hand figure  with a multiplying factor let's quickly  try out another problem say we have to  multiply 371 with 399 try it out we can  see that both numbers are pretty close  to 400 if 400 is the base then 100 is  the power of 10 we are looking at 10  squared and 100 times 4 is equal to 400  371 minus 400 is equal to minus twenty  nine and 399 minus 400 is equal to -1  based our deviations done some on the  left and the product on the right 371  minus 1 is equal to 370 and on the right  we will have minus 29 x minus 1 that  will be 29 as we have two zeros in the  base we need to have two digits on the  right so we write a 29 here this is not  our answer don't forget to multiply the  number on the left hand side with 4 we  multiply 370 with 4 and that equals 1480  and we get 29 down that's the correct  answer  371 times 399 is equal to 148 thousand  29 these were the exact  when the base is a multiple of power of  10 here it was a multiple of 10 squared  or 100 the only additional step here was  to multiply the number on the left hand  side with a multiplying factor we will  look at a couple of more examples in the  next part of the session
 

